        <item>
            <title>0.27.12</title>
            <pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 18:32:23 -0600</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>73</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.27.12</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>:root{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.45 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,system-ui,sans-serif;color:#1d1d1f;margin:0;padding:2px 4px}h3{font-size:13px;font-weight:600;margin:0 0 6px}ul{margin:0;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 4px}code{font:12px ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){body{color:#f5f5f7}}</style><h3>What's new in Keeploop 0.27.12</h3><ul><li>Mail monitors can target who a message was sent to: agents can use recipient_contains to match To, Cc, Delivered-To and X-Original-To, so plus addresses like name+tag@gmail.com work.</li><li>When an agent asks to delete a draft, you can now choose Always Allow: for one person, one domain or all drafts. All drafts includes drafts you wrote yourself, and a deleted draft cannot be recovered. You can remove the rule in Settings &gt; Permissions. Sending is unchanged.</li></ul>]]></description>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
